WitOS has no Linux system call instruction contract: ABI-1 differs in numbers, statuses and results, so musl's inline SVC stubs become calls into the system layer's dispatch (src/Substrate/libc), which maps each Linux call onto the kernel's. The vDSO names go: there is no vDSO, and musl's clock_gettime then uses the system call path.

